From d09cedcd86c05d01a5734eb305f0919dcaa12068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:07:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Galaxigans: pair every voice with the instrument it was given

Two mispairings, both silent, both the same mistake.

The sound effects named `v=6..8` for chip 2, which was right when `v=`
was zero-based and wrong once it was not: v=6 is chip 1, so the registers
were set on one chip while the notes sounded on another and every effect
played on default registers -- a pulse wave where noise was asked for.
The explosion stopped being an explosion and became a beep.

The motifs have the same fault at the source: written `[I:chip v=0]`
under `V:1` and `[I:chip v=1]` under `V:2`. One-based, `v=0` addresses no
voice at all, so every motif's lead has been losing its timbre silently
and its bass playing with the lead's. Generating them now shifts the
voice numbers up by one, so each voice gets its own instrument. That is
a deliberate correction of the material rather than a faithful copy of
it, and it is the first time these motifs have sounded as written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0117-galaxigans-pair-every-voice-with-the-instrument-it-was-given.patch fe0934fc43c4e31125fd7835a7bce7453cb6bc98d4bf83734f380faa43fdfc3e
